<title>USA: CME volume rises 13.3 pct to second highest Oct.</title>
<headline>CME volume rises 13.3 pct to second highest Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) said volume in October rose to 15,919,783 contracts, the second highest posting for the month of October in the exhange's history, after October 1994.</p>
<p>Volume was up 13.3 percent above the year-ago monthly level of 14,055,299 contracts.</p>
<p>Open interest at month's end stood at 6,505,411, up 14.8 percent from 5,664,976 at the end of October last year.</p>
<p>Year-to-date volume totalled 170,045,770, off 2.7 percent from 174,790,787 traded during the same nine months last year.  </p>
<p>Major categories were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   Oct 1996	% change	 Oct 1995</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   7,688,525	   +8.7	   7,072,295</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   462,277	   -6.2	     492,756</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   343,145	   -5.6	     363,440</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	    333,207	   +1.4	     328,533</p>
<p>  British pound	  209,828	  +61.5	     129,950</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	178,652	  -16.3	     213,504</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		1,648,954	   +1.4	   1,626,271</p>
<p>  Live cattle	    343,568	  +54.9	     221,841</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	 205,890	  +53.3	     134,280</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   2,171,168	 + 35.1	   1,607,061</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve  521,254	 +498.1		87,156</p>
<p>  British pound	  102,498	  -57.1	     238,949</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   171,255	  -15.3	     202,196</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   166,679	   -5.9	     177,112</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  447,389	  -17.7	     543,700</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     68,229	  +70.2		40,078</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for October 1996 totaled 15,919,783 and year-to-date volume stood at 170,045,770.</p>
